{
  "key": "oil-gas-pipeline",
  "name": "Gas Transmission Pipeline",
  "category": "mixed",
  "description": "A natural-gas transmission pipeline seen from the gas-control-centre SPAN: corporate IT (incl. gas-measurement analysts), a DMZ with a FortiGate SSL-VPN and a vendor jump host, the control centre (SCADA pair, historian, leak detection, gas measurement system, engineering) and five remote sites over VSAT (Hughes HT2000W, ~650 ms RTT) behind each terminal's NAT: two compressor stations (ControlLogix / Modicon M580 unit PLCs, SICAM A8000 RTUs on IEC 104, Emerson ROC800 flow computers, station HMIs, a turbine control panel) and three meter stations (ABB Totalflow / ROC800 flow computers, SCADAPack DNP3 RTUs). SCADA polls every 30-60 s and the gas measurement system pulls flow-computer history every 15 min, all heavily jittered. MS5 has a site-side sensor (nat local: true) so its flat LAN is visible. Planted findings: a vendor remote-access session into the compressor stations, a metering configuration write from a corporate PC, the flat MS5 station network, an EOL Windows 7 station HMI. Run: tgt run --env oil-gas-pipeline --pcap pipeline.pcap --once --rate 0",
  "options": {"snmp_community": "pl-n0c-ro"},
